{
  "sourceNullable": "{\"cells\":[{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"0c21d586\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"# LB 22.99 | invsqrt 101 - 62 qubits\\n\\n**Public leaderboard score:** 22.99252 for this circuit combination, submitted as a file. The previous v40 chemistry combination scored 22.98999.\\n\\nThe previous public invsqrt baseline by **busyaprime**, based on **mrmeows / team selenium**, used 63 qubits and cost about 102,349. Our modified circuit, developed with **GPT-6 Astra**, uses **62 qubits** and has an expected cost of **101,002.54** (about 1.32% lower). We reworked the encoded lookup, normalization and tail schedule while retaining the underlying phase map.\\n\\nThis builds on prior work. See [The Real $150K Was the Friends We Made](https://www.kaggle.com/code/manwithacat/the-real-150k-was-the-friends-we-made) and [busyaprime's circuit](https://www.kaggle.com/code/busyaprime/lb-22-86841-22x-cheaper-than-google-s-circuits). The archive records a full-domain 200,540,928-shot PASS using an independently built SDK. Actual leaderboard results can differ with the competition's hidden salt.\\n\\nChemistry uses the v44 candidate published by [Dmitrii Gluzdov](https://www.kaggle.com/code/dmitriigluzdov/quantum-circuit-compilation-from-source), building on earlier contributors. The official local verifier passed 78,080 shots; the cost is about 0.033% lower than our previous v40 chemistry.\\n\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"c9f75934\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":\"from pathlib import Path\\nfrom zipfile import ZipFile, ZIP_DEFLATED\\nimport hashlib\\n\\nbase_roots = [Path(\\\"/kaggle/input/qcc-2298-submission-20261030/submission\\\"),\\n              Path(\\\"/kaggle/input/datasets/yoyobar/qcc-2298-submission-20261030/submission\\\")]\\nchem_roots = [Path(\\\"/kaggle/input/qcc-chem-v44-20261030\\\"),\\n              Path(\\\"/kaggle/input/datasets/yoyobar/qcc-chem-v44-20261030\\\")]\\nbase = next((p for p in base_roots if p.is_dir()), None)\\nchem = next((p for p in chem_roots if p.is_dir()), None)\\nif base is None or chem is None:\\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\\\"Attach both submission datasets.\\\")\\n\\nexpected = {'invsqrt.kmb': 'a568bc79348165bad5be2349960d200300c5639ffd2142aca6d548e764a399d9', 'dqi.kmb': '7a378f4755605e0c5fa6117f808891bf8dcf0797d047155e6d4c9e75e3c99421', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_0.kmb': '6f516cba96b50d3e57b4c07574b1e4026f4392b8b904b6f82586d9a18b9f7a14', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_1.kmb': 'a4d90a649d9f0b0f0a0d21d476c74922d25094444c495f45403938ce0efe0287', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_10.kmb': 'fb89a6499c77e7e12ea1fadf371e3ab0a7428bdde35b5ff9c63b1d59291f2d58', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_11.kmb': '847b15fd034e55b64e3d507aa22ed40ce975e676847da5c00fe1a4b050e96bd1', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_12.kmb': '002a42f0ea763d5c62d4ec10fabafc3645ffa9fe5b057fec2624e6e95c199e86', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_13.kmb': '1e4a30a471bd12bb4090aed2572dd4564eeefd6b304a5462b7a3d3502906269f', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_14.kmb': 'ae2070998e31b7e05d01183914df20b6974c1760bddf90d1adac86ea75c7bf3f', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_2.kmb': '2e8dfdeb69c496e9e510fe99722153663760980d45c35ad9b72e79ba799dde49', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_3.kmb': '13817cf8d36ea112e62d7863edde2193aa5907dd0605612c4f0e1e54bacc173b', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_4.kmb': 'a2b685bcae6a1b0457c97389693935c44e0872f41add1abb4ab84caccfc754ab', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_5.kmb': '174f8ba8efda5aed6f3ec0fea5907e64491306e884b6e382ccc2e37161b1bc68', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_6.kmb': 'f9d2d34b97fd5db23a8d08591b8ebebb0a1b840678f6044065739023b26c9962', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_7.kmb': '3e4cafdd470f1cd35fa5f06bded8499ec3fa75be1951a2b7cf67f563558e94b4', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_8.kmb': '6e6aaa69b8a4785efbd2802f4f0490da30fba5ab73224c6fca08f5c398e07fd5', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_9.kmb': '4c21fff2c8285342a3da9f1484252678962dfc9fd389b751fb9568c47b22a272', 'dfthcsos/submission.npz': '95026d23e8b5b117991df008f1defefa62459343d8e24994486760ae499841e4'}\\nfiles = {name: (chem / Path(name).name if name.startswith(\\\"dfthcsos/\\\") else base / name)\\n         for name in expected}\\ntemporary = Path(\\\"/kaggle/working/submission.tmp\\\")\\ntry:\\n    with ZipFile(temporary, \\\"w\\\", compression=ZIP_DEFLATED, compresslevel=1) as archive:\\n        for name, path in sorted(files.items()):\\n            digest = hashlib.sha256()\\n            with path.open(\\\"rb\\\") as file:\\n                for chunk in iter(lambda: file.read(8 * 1024 * 1024), b\\\"\\\"):\\n                    digest.update(chunk)\\n            if digest.hexdigest() != expected[name]:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Unexpected input hash: {name}\\\")\\n            archive.write(path, name)\\n    output = Path(\\\"/kaggle/working/submission.zip\\\")\\n    temporary.replace(output)\\nexcept Exception:\\n    temporary.unlink(missing_ok=True)\\n    raise\\nprint(\\\"Ready for submission:\\\", output)\\nprint(\\\"Components: invsqrt Q62, DQI, chemistry v44; all 18 input hashes matched.\\\")\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\"}},\"nbformat\":4,\"nbformat_minor\":5}",
